From 71baf71e8940f435c8351f0a395bc50808d455e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Apr 2026 12:50:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] epoll-kqueue shim: fix EPOLL_CTL_MOD and use
 edge-triggered mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summary:
## Problem 1: EPOLL_CTL_MOD leaves stale filters

kqueue uses separate filters for read (`EVFILT_READ`) and write
(`EVFILT_WRITE`), unlike epoll which has a single event mask per fd.
The macOS epoll shim implemented `EPOLL_CTL_MOD` as just `EV_ADD`,
which adds new filters but never removes old ones:

```
 Linux epoll                      macOS kqueue shim (before fix)
      |                                    |
 CTL_ADD(EPOLLIN|EPOLLOUT)         EV_ADD EVFILT_READ
      |                            EV_ADD EVFILT_WRITE
      |                                    |
 CTL_MOD(EPOLLIN)                  EV_ADD EVFILT_READ
      |                            (EVFILT_WRITE still registered!)
      |                                    |
 epoll_wait: only EPOLLIN          kevent: EPOLLIN + spurious EPOLLOUT
```

This causes spurious EPOLLOUT events for connections that were modified
to only listen for EPOLLIN, waking up the daemon unnecessarily.

## Fix 1

Delete both `EVFILT_READ` and `EVFILT_WRITE` before re-adding the
requested filters. Errors from deletion are ignored since the filter
may not have been previously registered.

## Problem 2: Level-triggered kqueue causes spin loops

Linux epoll is level-triggered by default, and the vsock daemon's code
relies on this working correctly. However, kqueue's level-triggered
behavior on listener sockets is more aggressive — it refires
`EVFILT_READ` on every `kevent()` call while connections are pending
in the backlog, even if the caller hasn't called `accept()` yet. This
causes tight spin loops in the daemon's `process_backend_evt` path.

## Fix 2

Use `EV_CLEAR` (kqueue's edge-triggered equivalent) on all filter
registrations by default. This makes kqueue report each state change
once, matching the practical behavior that the daemon code expects.
`EV_CLEAR` was previously only applied when `EPOLLET` was explicitly
requested, but the daemon never requests it.

Test Plan:
Rebuilt vhost_device_vsock. Verified daemon no longer spins on startup
when host proxies connect before vring initialization.

